message: "Please cite this work and the original data and method sources."
title: "Painter Street Overpass response analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kumar
    given-names: Utpal
    affiliation: "Berkeley Seismological Laboratory, University of California, Berkeley"
  - family-names: Mosalam
    given-names: Khalid M.
    affiliation: "Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering and Pacific Earthquake Engineering Research Center, University of California, Berkeley"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Analysis of earthquake response at the Painter Street Overpass in Rio Dell,
  California, using derived measurements from 22 earthquakes during 2012-2024
  and National Bridge Inventory inspection records. The code computes response
  features, fits the relationship between modal frequency and input amplitude,
  and tests for persistent frequency shifts after amplitude adjustment.
  Response departures do not establish earthquake damage or its absence.
  The package starts from derived measurements and does not repeat waveform
  processing or modal identification. Code is MIT-licensed; original
  documentation, figures, and derived tables are CC BY 4.0, subject to source
  notices.
repository-code: "https://github.com/earthinversion/painter-street-analysis"
keywords:
  - structural health monitoring
  - bridge response
  - modal frequency
  - earthquake engineering
  - reproducible research
